camchrome: screen.colorDepth is 24 or 30, never 32.

The persona drew colorDepth 32 for 4% of seeds. Chrome reports 24, or 30 on a 10-bit display,
never 32, and the CSS color media feature (bits per colour channel) cannot decompose 32 (Clearcote
audit: "screen.colorDepth decomposes into the CSS color media feature", found with a seed the
development runs did not use). The former 32 entry of the weighted table now draws 24, so every
other seed keeps exactly the persona it had; an imported capture's 32 reads as 24; the
validator accepts {24, 30} only.

--- a/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.cc
+++ b/components/ungoogled/persona_profile.cc
@@ -185,10 +185,13 @@
 // Color depth: Win11 desktops are overwhelmingly 24; HDR / multi-monitor can be
 // 30/32. Keep 24 dominant so a Windows persona never reports the rare value too
 // often (which is itself a tell).
+// camchrome (1012): Chrome reports screen.colorDepth 24, or 30 on a 10-bit display, never 32
+// (the CSS color media feature is bits per channel, and 32 does not divide into three). The
+// former 32 entry now draws 24, so every other seed keeps exactly the persona it had.
 constexpr std::array<WeightedEntry<unsigned>, 3> kColorDepths = {{
     {24u, 0.92},
     {30u, 0.04},
-    {32u, 0.04},
+    {24u, 0.04},
 }};
 
 // Windows consumer GPU pool (ANGLE/D3D11 strings). Index 0 (Intel UHD 770) is
@@ -372,7 +375,10 @@
     if (auto v = s->FindInt("height")) p->screen_height = *v;
     if (auto v = s->FindInt("avail_width")) p->avail_screen_width = *v;
     if (auto v = s->FindInt("avail_height")) p->avail_screen_height = *v;
-    if (auto v = s->FindInt("color_depth")) p->color_depth = *v;
+    if (auto v = s->FindInt("color_depth")) {
+      // camchrome (1012): a capture's 32 is what Chrome reports as 24.
+      p->color_depth = *v == 32 ? 24 : *v;
+    }
     if (auto v = num(*s, "device_pixel_ratio")) p->device_pixel_ratio = *v;
   }
   if (const base::DictValue* w = d.FindDictByDottedPath("webgl.webgl1")) {
